<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">12 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 12 August, from 1099 to 2000.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1099">1099 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">927 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Crusaders defeat a Fatimid army at Ascalon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A month after taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, the crusaders surprised and routed an Egyptian relief army near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashkelon">Ascalon</a>. The victory, the last battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>, secured the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> kingdom.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1759">1759 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">267 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Frederick the Great is crushed at Kunersdorf</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Russian and Austrian army destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a>'s Prussian force near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> an der Oder. Frederick wrote that all was lost, but his enemies failed to follow up and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> survived.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Frederick II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1851">1851 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">175 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Isaac Singer patents his improved sewing machine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Isaac Singer received a US patent for a sewing machine with an up-and-down needle and foot treadle. Sold on instalment plans, Singer machines brought sewing machines into homes worldwide.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1944">1944 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">82 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">SS troops massacre villagers at Sant'Anna di Stazzema</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/waffen-ss">Waffen-SS</a> soldiers killed some 560 civilians, many of them women and children, in the Tuscan village of Sant'Anna di Stazzema. It was one of the worst atrocities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy">German occupation of Italy</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-occupation-of-italy">German occupation of Italy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1981">1981 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">45 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">IBM launches its Personal Computer</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">IBM unveiled the IBM PC model 5150, running Microsoft's MS-DOS. Its open design was widely copied, and 'PC compatible' machines came to dominate business and home computing.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/2000">2000 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">26 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Russian submarine Kursk sinks in the Barents Sea</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Explosions in its torpedo compartment sent the nuclear submarine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kursk">Kursk</a> to the seabed, killing all 118 crew. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s slow response and refusal of early foreign help caused national anger.</p></div></li></ol>
